Podman (run OCI-based containers in pods)

Podman provides a command to manage containers.

* Supports OCI and Docker image formats
* Supports multiple means to download images and verify images
* Container image management
* Full management of container lifecycle
* Support for pods to manage groups of containers together
* Resource isolation of containers and pods

IMPORTANT: After installation, you MUST manually configure Slackware
to use cgroups v2, and then add UID and GID space for your user!

If you fail to do this, Podman will not run!

Detailed instructions for configuration are in the
`README.Slackware` document in `/usr/doc/podman-*`
